{"title":"2026 Indonesia District MO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Note that this is also known as the <i>OSN Tingkat Kota</i>, or <i>OSN-K</i>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Basic_Ability\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Basic Ability</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Advanced_Ability\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Advanced Ability</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Basic_Ability\">Basic Ability</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Basic Ability\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> that satisfies the equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb7cd17d0cd32dbf754496646ef8de10be4ce5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x-y=1 \\qquad y-z=2 \\qquad xyz=77\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"16\" />\nFind the value of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb4651a76cb1e20a6011fbe27b95369f62f22aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{yz}+\\frac{y}{xz}+\\frac{z}{xy}-\\left( \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}\\right) = \\dots\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"43\" />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Andi, Budi, and Cici plays a game by coin flipping. The order they play in starts from Andi, then Budi, then Cici. The first player who flips heads will win. If all of them get tails, the game cycles back, and they play again in the same order. If the probability that Andi wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa4d49561e5a15aba0babbcfa6218089f9944fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" />, the probability that Budi wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d14b1ade917f5331a1143fbcab1ee488b0ebb943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"39\" />, the probability that Cici wins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/17156473988d544f5800e12e64daeab6dd69d223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe1842d9f07bba882135b6497ffb1173ec75297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> are relatively prime integers, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aeda4a84d017f23d30e106b1e85aa97af86f4861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The polynomial\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e876e86acd744066aee265d810d8d0186d0dde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x)=x^3+ax^2+bx+c\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" />\nis divisble by the polynomial\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b137b97b6bfbfeaad8d5646084f18ef9cf0a80c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(x)=x^2+\\frac{1}{40}\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" />\nFind the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8362dd17da7c07cedd4018d589a0b21e9575e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of a right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If the circumradius of this triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the inradius of this triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, where r can be written in the form:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4d941e3801f3da426530a82aa5e5d5e6ccb9de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=\\sqrt{m}+n\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f506cc197a19861e22182e78e75b9072be3ebb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The amount of integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1437ad45f3a23e5d6ff330cdc6771b378d0ff047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$456$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive that can be written as a number with increasing digits from left to right is...\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> be the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d3d5e9f45e6798cae12e334c6fb43d67a91fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d03af3d43ad5652b0ab9dc7deec092c9943b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall \\, n\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d00d45c7f72de91ddae31751503f0a62a4210f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=0, a_2=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" />, find the value of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/2371cd3244d0b68c2b8e15d1d1082bba10f5c14d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{2026} a_i\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alda has a suitcase locked behind an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit combination code that only contains the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8480bbc71e3fd12e3f8b749c49c06897ee7bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,4,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. It is also known that the combination code contains exactly one digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and four digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. How many combination codes satisfy these conditions?\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given prime numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/3674de20e2b78b5790ea714b9dcaa11af6aa2340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q,r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> that satisfy:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5de78bb2a30815698cbc0bff92b2d5ff3f0c82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p+q+r=26\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8160fcf6beccbf67d689256b62b8be66d9dae9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[pq + qr + pr=191\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />\nFind the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63795f5ae81b5558afc51ffd1b2e8a7a30d38f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed59715543cb33b872cdc2223cea870166200919.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(15mm);  size(5cm, 0);  pair A = (0,0); pair B = (4,0); pair C = (4,4); pair D = (0,4);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(1pt) + black); draw(arc(D, 4, 0, -90), linewidth(1pt) + black); draw(arc((2,0), 2, 0, 180), linewidth(1pt)+black); draw(circle((3.2,0.64),0.64),linewidth(1pt)+black); draw((3.2,0.64)--(3.2,0),linewidth(1pt)+black); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NW); label(&quot;300&quot;,(2,0),S); label(&quot;300&quot;,(0,2),W); label(&quot;$r$&quot;,(3.2,0.32),E); [/asy]\" width=\"345\" height=\"328\" /></center>\n<p>A circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is externally tangent to a quarter circle inscribed in a square with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, and is internally tangent to an inscribed semicircle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e10e5f3aa7c766cb27c3ad319fa526f71588cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, as shown in the figure above. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The roots of the quadratic function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/5514bbe4b865e0e3e8ea184e4f5722fd5dbf05e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=x^2+px+q^2\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />\nare integers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are prime numbers, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd790111eee5c5b02558911a11d92cb15760a47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+2q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Advanced_Ability\">Advanced Ability</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Advanced Ability\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/6730a33129854d9bc3e015a4f604aa825bc17ff6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+\\lfloor x \\rfloor = \\lfloor x^2 \\rfloor + x +\\frac{31}{100}\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />\nIf the largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies this equation that is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p><small>(Question re-phrased from the original question to remove ambiguity)</small>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle is divided into a grid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b2acbb14d3d8c3be4519bb070578c630129e2bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> squares. Each square is to be colored either black or white, subject to the following conditions: every column must contain at least one black square, and every row must contain at least one black square as well as at least one white square. Furthermore, each white square is to be filled with a number from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/0/df03ebb613fbce0d34e449d2577fcfbd8227e448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,2,3,4,5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> such that the sum of the numbers in each row is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. How many ways can the coloring and filling be performed to satisfy these procedures?\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c2cebdbc524624cf9bab853640b2d6e8b00320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, The minimum value of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa22800c9dc909617ff7be5875dc7131a461ad2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+50y+\\frac{625}{xy^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"116\" height=\"42\" /> is achieved at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/f/dff3b56795afc9981c804f07bd528186b6e4d7f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa416ed9edf5c273410def99cd1782b125b4a08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider an equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17aa122e7df8cbf3b28f6a1f1356f31fafd9489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M\\neq N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is placed inside the triangle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/987ce132ede87a548bf85aec6e0b852dc814a981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DMN$\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is also an equilateral triangle. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> intersects side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> on point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> intersects side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7eeccf6699de3213af9d9ebd90486b853c8f1d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MN}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fad9e2376e0c05591aee1c882ad89dcc950792f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BF}=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f12eec7ea7e5660201ebc01e343cf28c2fc643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CE}=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, what is the side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> denote the sum of all positive factors of an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the value of the sum of all natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb377f6ff79e5147160fb99c7a0e45abfc15a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is odd.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two circles centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> intersect at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. An external common tangent intersects the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, given that the tangent is closer to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> than point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The extension of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/95915f5885ed19f737ac8338c7c0b1d0e23fb73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XY}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the radius of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e612de4c5d7cb6cb4ca60af3bef7e1fd0d52e0c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{O_1 O_2} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"21\" />, find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f4d76287869027a55c26559d6290daad324954.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle O_1 P O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_16\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0d7aaf739a80169398658fae3762d21329172ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\overline{AD}}{\\overline{DB}}=\\frac{7}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"73\" height=\"44\" />, and a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec911147545b83dada86c676849da6d5e8734a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\overline{AE}}{\\overline{EC}} = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"72\" height=\"44\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41ee10c07baa91f100ec2eeca6b7b6ed3ab86698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/699784c989c3db382520e6f92819e062d239f504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db52454ec9c8dee6c90b1a3ccd42965fedf44951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_17\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the following binomial coefficient equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d827ff0e18b271f45e0e7f6eb55d4bc1edd127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 \\binom{m}{k} + 3\\binom{n}{k+1}=48z\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"53\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a7089e0ef5c753553634923a3c4c569e75788405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,k,n,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> are positive integers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is minimized, find the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_18\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a sequence of rational numbers that consists of the following terms:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/72785a823d95f5bb0c725505dcad6edeeb96d72f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\frac{1}{567}, -\\frac{1}{566}, \\dots, -\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{2}, \\dots, \\frac{1}{565}, \\frac{1}{566}, \\frac{1}{567}.\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"37\" />\nAndi plays a game where each move, he selects 2 distinct numbers from the sequence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and replaces it with 1 number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c8baca6250da65a6859bb60e3e7f0678a1a6e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y-xy)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" />. After a sequence of moves, the sequence eventually will only have a single number. If that number was written in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_19\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the sum of the tenths and the unit digit of the expression:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae27f0a6342f89d1880258a24e73751e9b9fa30e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(6+\\sqrt{26}\\right)^{18}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems/Problem_20\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_Indonesia_District_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_District_MO\">Indonesia District MO</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071246\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 679/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expans